  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nLatest global model and numerical guidance are illustrating a H500\nridge developing with its extent into the central Plains, with a\nseries of mid level disturbances traversing the central Rockies\nfrom WSW to ENE. Data also shows a sub-tropical tie to the main\nmoisture transport going through the middle of the coming week \nwith these disturbances. Coupled with daytime heating, we could \nsee several chances of showers and storms. With PWAT values in \nthe 99th percentile and quite limited overall steering flow, \ntraining storms with flooding potential will be watched closely as\nwe go mid to later this week. Overall high temperatures in the \nlong term forecast period will remain below average before \nreturning to near average by the first half of the coming weekend.",
